<% if (includeMdDocs) { -%>

### Generating Markdown Docs

`npm run docs` regenerates `docs/` (per-module + per-model pages) by scanning source.
**Request bodies and query params are auto-derived** from the Joi schemas referenced by
`validateBody(...)` / `validateQuery(...)`, and **responses are inferred** from the
controller → service → model chain (single → `{ item }`, list → paginated, etc.). So you
normally write only `@doc` + an optional `@desc`:

```<%= ext %>
// @doc Create example | 201
// @desc Creates a new example and returns it.
router.post('/', validateBody(createExampleSchema), ctrl.create);
```

Overrides (only when inference can't reach): `// @body <json>`, `// @query <text>`,
`// @response <code> <json>`. The shared engine in `src/utils/doc-introspect.<%= ext %>` powers
both `npm run docs` and the Swagger UI, so they never drift. Run `npm run docs -- --check`
in CI to fail when docs are stale. Models need no annotation — fields, enums, `ref`
relationships and indexes come from the Mongoose schema.

